SUMMARY

  Implemented ROADMAP.md Milestone 7 for Tamlinux 0.7.0 Northern Torch while
  working around active claims in libtam, tam-view, tam-knox, tam-clam, tam,
  and improvements-fred-tamlinux (leaving components.lock untouched):
  - Added tam-pane Unix domain socket IPC support to
    src/desktop/shell/host/hyprland_backend.py when TAM_PANE_SOCKET is set and
    HYPRLAND_INSTANCE_SIGNATURE is unset (monitors, monitors-all, workspaces,
    active-workspace, devices, binds, config-errors, rollinglog,
    select-output-workspace, focus-workspace, focus-output, move-window,
    move-workspace, dpms, batch, reload), preserving Hyprland behavior and
    refresh-rate fallback (60 Hz when headless outputs report 0).
  - Forwarded TAM_PANE_SOCKET in closed child environments:
    src/desktop/shell/host/BarApi.qml,
    src/desktop/plugins/fred.workspaces/Workspaces.qml,
    src/desktop/plugins/fred.monitor/Panel.qml,
    src/desktop/plugins/fred.monitor/fred-monitor-layout (spawn_guard),
    src/desktop/plugins/fred.keyboard/BarWidget.qml, and
    src/desktop/plugins/fred.clock/Panel.qml.
  - Updated src/desktop/plugins/fred.monitor/fred-monitor-layout to format
    tp.monitor(...) rules and persist atomically to
    ~/.config/tamlinux/tam-pane/monitors.lua when running under tam-pane.
  - Updated src/desktop/shell/services/clipboard/paste-text.sh to detect
    focused tam-last windows via tam-pane msg windows (pane:<id>) and paste
    via tam-pane msg dispatch send_key Ctrl+Shift+V with focus-change abort.
  - Guarded Hyprland-only hyprctl calls in
    src/commands/tam-launch-about/tam-launch-about under tam-pane.
  - Extended tests/test_clipboard_paste.py with tam-pane cases and added
    tests/test_tam_pane_shell_proof.py proving the backend, plugin helpers,
    real Quickshell + all nine shipped fred.* plugins over native Wayland on
    headless two-output tam-pane 0.2.8, tam-last + tam-clam, tam-edit PTY
    save, and tam-launch-about with Hyprland stopped.

